  <dashboards>
    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder="true" name="A Trend Model Comparison">
      <style />
      <size maxheight="1000" maxwidth="1200" minheight="1000" minwidth="1200" sizing-mode="fixed" />
      <zones>
        <zone h="100000" id="1" type-v2="layout-basic" w="100000" x="0" y="0">
          <zone h="6598" id="2" type-v2="text" w="100000" x="0" y="0">
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold="true" fontcolor="#333333" fontname="Arial" fontsize="18">A Trend Model Comparison | 2021–2024</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h="5076" id="6" type-v2="text" w="32653" x="0" y="8121">
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold="false" fontcolor="#333333" fontname="Arial" fontsize="11">Linear | R² .000119; p .941331</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h="63960" id="7" name="A1 Linear Trend" show-title="false" w="32653" x="0" y="13197">
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h="5076" id="8" type-v2="text" w="32653" x="33673" y="8121">
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold="false" fontcolor="#333333" fontname="Arial" fontsize="11">Exponential | R² .0000658; p .956361</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h="63960" id="9" name="A2 Exponential Trend" show-title="false" w="32653" x="33673" y="13197">
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h="5076" id="10" type-v2="text" w="32654" x="67346" y="8121">
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold="false" fontcolor="#333333" fontname="Arial" fontsize="11">Quadratic (2) | R² .011061; p .778603</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h="63960" id="11" name="A3 Polynomial Trend" show-title="false" w="32654" x="67346" y="13197">
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h="20305" id="90" type-v2="text" w="100000" x="0" y="79695">
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold="false" fontcolor="#333333" fontname="Arial" fontsize="11">I compared all three trend models using the same 48 monthly Sales totals, January 2021 to December 2024. Tableau Describe Trend Model reports linear R-squared 0.000119 (p = 0.941331), exponential R-squared 0.0000658 (p = 0.956361), and degree-2 polynomial R-squared 0.011061 (p = 0.778603). The quadratic has the largest historical R-squared on the Sales scale, but it explains only about 1.1% of variation and none of the model p-values is below 0.05. The exponential model fits ln(Sales), so its R-squared and error units are not directly comparable with the two untransformed models. I would use the simple linear fit as a descriptive baseline rather than plan for growth from the small quadratic curve; seasonal planning is more defensible than claiming a meaningful long-run trend.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid="{51C1650E-A98E-4CC7-B2F0-DDAA3F15B508}" />
    </dashboard>
    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder="true" name="B Distribution Findings">
      <style />
      <size maxheight="1000" maxwidth="1200" minheight="1000" minwidth="1200" sizing-mode="fixed" />
      <zones>
        <zone h="100000" id="1" type-v2="layout-basic" w="100000" x="0" y="0">
          <zone h="6091" id="2" type-v2="text" w="100000" x="0" y="0">
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor="#333333" fontname="Arial" fontsize="18">B Distribution Findings | Monthly Region–Category records</run>
            </formatted-text>
          </zone>
          <zone h="32488" id="3" type-v2="text" w="100000" x="0" y="67512">
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor="#333333" fontname="Arial" fontsize="11">Each point is one monthly Region-Category record, with 192 points in each category pane and 576 overall. The bands mark mean Profit plus or minus one and two sample standard deviations within that category; the labeled Average line identifies the center. Furniture has mean monthly Profit $106,375 and SD $11,614, Office Supplies $107,510 and $11,828, and Technology $107,877 and $11,166, so Technology has the highest mean and narrowest spread, although the three distributions overlap considerably. There are 6 Furniture, 10 Office Supplies and 11 Technology marks outside their respective two-SD limits, which are review candidates rather than proof of errors or a normal distribution.

SD boundaries by category are listed in Written Notes. Bands: mean ±1 and ±2 sample SD; line: average Profit. Category panes use the same axes.</run>
            </formatted-text>
          </zone>
          <zone h="58883" id="4" name="B Profit Distributions" show-title="false" w="100000" x="0" y="7106" />
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid="{30998EEC-3549-474D-ABA2-D9916493416F}" />
    </dashboard>
    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder="true" name="C Cluster Findings">
      <style />
      <size maxheight="1000" maxwidth="1200" minheight="1000" minwidth="1200" sizing-mode="fixed" />
      <zones>
        <zone h="100000" id="1" type-v2="layout-basic" w="100000" x="0" y="0">
          <zone h="6091" id="2" type-v2="text" w="100000" x="0" y="0">
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor="#333333" fontname="Arial" fontsize="18">C Cluster Findings | Monthly Region–Category records</run>
            </formatted-text>
          </zone>
          <zone h="37564" id="3" type-v2="text" w="100000" x="0" y="62436">
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor="#333333" fontname="Arial" fontsize="11">Tableau k-means uses four clusters, with SUM(Sales), SUM(Profit), and SUM(Customers) as the three inputs, for all 576 monthly Region-Category records and no unclustered marks. The centers separate lower-sales/lower-profit records (Clusters 1 and 2) from higher-sales/higher-profit records (Clusters 3 and 4), with customer counts distinguishing groups within those pairs. Cluster 1 has more recorded customers than Cluster 2 but only modestly higher Sales, so I would investigate product mix and conversion before recommending more traffic. Cluster 3 combines higher Sales and Profit with the most customers, while Cluster 4 achieves similar Sales and Profit with fewer recorded customers, making the two useful comparisons for staffing and sales-mix reviews. These are groups of monthly operating records, not individual customer segments, and the simulated daily customer counts are summed rather than deduplicated people.

Cluster centers (n | Sales | Profit | Customers):
1: 147 | $580,030 | $98,088 | 3,771.4     2: 108 | $563,070 | $98,470 | 3,389.2
3: 158 | $639,030 | $114,950 | 3,863.4     4: 163 | $637,460 | $113,880 | 3,485.6
Within SS 21.323; between SS 30.510. See Written Notes for diagnostics and cautions.</run>
            </formatted-text>
          </zone>
          <zone h="53807" id="4" name="C Four Clusters" show-title="false" w="78350" x="0" y="7106" />
          <zone h="22335" id="102" name="C Four Clusters" pane-specification-id="0" param="[federated.module8retail].[none:AdhocCluster:1:ok]" type-v2="color" w="19073" x="80927" y="9644" />
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid="{22BEE92C-E13F-4983-A623-EDFF2D36DE33}" />
    </dashboard>
    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder="true" name="D Forecast Comparison">
      <style />
      <size maxheight="1000" maxwidth="1200" minheight="1000" minwidth="1200" sizing-mode="fixed" />
      <zones>
        <zone h="100000" id="1" type-v2="layout-basic" w="100000" x="0" y="0">
          <zone h="6598" id="2" type-v2="text" w="100000" x="0" y="0">
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold="true" fontcolor="#333333" fontname="Arial" fontsize="18">D Forecast Comparison | History 2021–24; forecast 2025</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h="5076" id="6" type-v2="text" w="100000" x="0" y="8121">
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold="false" fontcolor="#333333" fontname="Arial" fontsize="11">Automatic | no trend; multiplicative season | RMSE $156,756; AIC 1,178</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h="24366" id="7" name="D1 Automatic Forecast" show-title="false" w="100000" x="0" y="13197">
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h="5076" id="8" type-v2="text" w="100000" x="0" y="40609">
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold="false" fontcolor="#333333" fontname="Arial" fontsize="11">Custom | additive trend + season | RMSE $155,611; AIC 1,182</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h="24365" id="9" name="D2 Custom Seasonal Forecast" show-title="false" w="100000" x="0" y="45685">
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h="28427" id="90" type-v2="text" w="100000" x="0" y="71573">
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold="false" fontcolor="#333333" fontname="Arial" fontsize="11">Both native forecasts use all 48 monthly Sales totals from January 2021 to December 2024 and project January to December 2025, with no final periods ignored, a 12-month seasonal cycle and 95% prediction intervals. Automatic selects a multiplicative level, no trend and multiplicative seasonality, while Custom uses additive level, additive trend and additive seasonality. Describe Forecast reports fitted RMSE $156,756, MAE $127,826, MAPE 1.8% and AIC 1,178 for Automatic, compared with $155,611, $127,417, 1.8% and 1,182 for Custom. Although Custom reduces RMSE by $1,145 (about 0.73%), I prefer Automatic as the planning baseline because its lower AIC favors the simpler no-trend model and Part A gives little support for a sustained trend. Both retain a low February and high March seasonal pattern, which may partly reflect the number of selling days rather than changes in daily demand. These are fitted diagnostics, not a held-out forecasting test, and the four annual cycles, absent promotions/pricing/external events, and model-dependent intervals limit confidence in the future projections.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr="border-color" value="#000000" />
              <format attr="border-style" value="none" />
              <format attr="border-width" value="0" />
              <format attr="margin" value="8" />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid="{C17F7FA5-9B87-400C-82F8-973F5FF416F5}" />
    </dashboard>
